   "body": {
    "en": "range(start, stop, step) produces a sequence of integers that begins at start, increases by step, and stops before stop: the stop value is never included. start defaults to 0 and step to 1, so range(5) gives 0, 1, 2, 3, 4. A negative step counts down: range(10, 0, -2) gives 10, 8, 6, 4, 2. The step cannot be zero."
   },
   "points": [
